 "tagline": "My everyday life, my cares, my possibilities.",
 "description": "Sort my world by where and with whom I live, what I care about, my past, my present and the paths open to me.",
 "inspiration": "Original: In Being and Time, Heidegger describes human existence as being-in-the-world: we always find ourselves among places, tools and other people, already caring about things. Our existence is temporal — shaped by what has been and stretched toward possibilities — and can be lived “authentically”, owning our choices rather than simply doing what “one” does.\n\nMinest adaptation: this template turns those ideas into everyday areas: my everyday world, my relationships, my concerns, my past, my present, my possibilities and choices that are my own. It is not a template about death, and it never asks you to think about it.",
