  ],
  "original": "Original: In Being and Time, Heidegger describes human existence as being-in-the-world: we always find ourselves among places, tools and other people, already caring about things. Our existence is temporal — shaped by what has been and stretched toward possibilities — and can be lived “authentically”, owning our choices rather than simply doing what “one” does.",
